{"name":"Robotic Gods","hex":"#94a2b1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"robotic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, relating to, or resembling a robot; mechanical, lacking emotion or personality, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/robotic"},{"term":"gods","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of god"]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Ellipsis of oh gods."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gods"}],"entries":[{"title":"Robotics","blocks":[{"text":"Robotics is the interdisciplinary study and practice of the design, construction, operation, and use of robots. A roboticist is someone who specializes in robotics. Robotics usually combines four aspects of design work: a power source, mechanical construction, a control system, and software."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Puma_Robotic_Arm_-_GPN-2000-001817.jpg/330px-Puma_Robotic_Arm_-_GPN-2000-001817.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robotics"},{"title":"Deity","blocks":[{"text":"A deity is a supernatural being considered to have authority over some aspect of the universe and/or life, with many also being considered as sacred and worthy of worship. It is \"a spirit or being believed to have created, or to control some part of the universe or life, for which such a deity is often worshipped\". The Oxford Dictionary of English explains deity as being anything revered as divine; while C. Scott Littleton defines a deity as \"a being with powers greater than those of ordinary humans, but who interacts with humans, positively or negatively, in ways that carry humans to new levels of consciousness, beyond the grounded preoccupations of ordinary life\". A male deity is called a god, while a female deity is called a goddess."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Maler_der_Grabkammer_der_Nefertari_001.jpg/330px-Maler_der_Grabkammer_der_Nefertari_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deity"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/PIA19664-MarsInSightLander-Assembly-20150430.jpg/500px-PIA19664-MarsInSightLander-Assembly-20150430.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/PIA19664-MarsInSightLander-Assembly-20150430.jpg/1280px-PIA19664-MarsInSightLander-Assembly-20150430.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/PIA19664-MarsInSightLander-Assembly-20150430.jpg/500px-PIA19664-MarsInSightLander-Assembly-20150430.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The InSight lander with solar panels","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APIA19664-MarsInSightLander-Assembly-20150430.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/2005-11-14_ShadowLeg_Finished_medium.jpg/500px-2005-11-14_ShadowLeg_Finished_medium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/2005-11-14_ShadowLeg_Finished_medium.jpg/500px-2005-11-14_ShadowLeg_Finished_medium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A robotic leg powered by air muscles","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2005-11-14_ShadowLeg_Finished_medium.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Mantis_Walking_Machine.jpg/500px-Mantis_Walking_Machine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Mantis_Walking_Machine.jpg/500px-Mantis_Walking_Machine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campa